Shop\nL147: \nL148: 【2†Close】 【2†Back】 【2†Close】\nL149: \nL150: ### In this section\nL151: \nL152:   * 【3†Shop home†www.shop.parliament.uk】\nL153: \nL154: 【57†UK Parliament】\nL155: # The Lord Speaker\nL156: \nL157: The Lord Speaker chairs daily business in the House of Lords chamber from his seat on the Woolsack. He also acts as an ambassador for the Lords and chairs the Commission which provides high-level strategic and political direction for the Lords Administration.\nL158: \nL159: The post of Lord Speaker was established in 2006. Lord Forsyth of Drumlean was elected by Lords members in 2026 to a five-year term as the fifth Lord Speaker.\nL160: 【58†Image: There is no description available for this image (ID: 211425)】\nL161: \nL162: 【58†Image: Reflection of image】\nL163: \nL164: 【59†The Lord Speaker's role】\nL165: \nL166: The Lord Speaker presides over work in the Lords chamber and acts as an ambassador for the House.\nL167: \nL168: 【60†About Lord Forsyth of Drumlean】\nL169: \nL170: Find out more about the Lord Speaker, Lord Forsyth of Drumlean\nL171: \nL172: 【61†Lord Speaker's Lectures】\nL173: The Lord Speaker’s Lecture series has run since 2010, providing members of the House of Lords and external experts with a forum to deliver lectures and answer questions on their specialist subjects or topics of interest.\nL174: \nL175: 【62†Lord Speaker's Events】\nL176: \nL177: The Lord Speaker attends many events as a representative of the House of Lords.\nL178: \nL179: 【63†History of the Lord Speaker's Role】\nL180: The Lord Speaker presides over the House of Lords as well as chairing the House of Lords Commission and acting as an ambassador for the Upper House of the UK Parliament.\nL181: \nL182: 【64†Lord Speaker in the news】\nL183: \nL184: In his role as an ambassador for the House of Lords, the Lord Speaker makes occasional appearances in the media.\nL185: \nL186: 【65†Lord Speaker speeches】\nL187: \nL188: Sharing expertise and working to broaden understanding about the work and role of the Lords.\nL189: 【66†The Lord Speaker's travel, gift and official entertainment registers】\nL190: \nL191: The Lord Speaker's policy is to publish transparency data covering many aspects of his role.\nL192: ## 【67†Lords engagement programme】\nL193: \nL194: The House of Lords engagement programme aims to reach out to the public and engage with them about what the House of Lords does and how it works for them.\nL195: \nL196: Related Links\nL197: \nL198:   * 【68†View all Lord Speaker news】\nL199:   * 【65†Lord Speaker speeches】\nL200:   * 【69†Former Lord Speakers】\nL201:   * 【63†History of the Lord Speaker's Role】\nL202: ## Lord Speaker news\nL203: 【70†Lords completes examination of Cyber Security and Resilience Bill Network and information systems resilience bill has third reading.\nL204: Find out more 30 October 2026】 【71†Leading historian Peter Hennessy Lord Hennessy of Nympsfield, is the latest guest on Lord Speaker’s Corner as he shares candid insights on power, public service and challenges facing modern politics 14 October 2026】 【72†Lord Forsyth's speech to the Hansard Society Read the Lord Speaker's speech to the Hansard Society, given on 16 July 2026 17 July 2026】 【73†Lord Forsyth's address to National Parliamentary Prayer Breakfast Read the Lord Speaker's address to the National Parliamentary Prayer Breakfast on July 7 2026 in Westminster Hall.\nL205: 14 July 2026】\nL206: ## Contact the Lord Speaker\nL207: \nL208: The Rt Hon the Lord Forsyth of Drumlean\nL209: \nL210: House of Lords\nL211: London\nL212: SW1A 0PW\nL213: \nL214: Journalists should contact Sarah Womack, Senior Communications Officer\nL215: Email: womacks@parliament.uk\nL216: \nL217: ## River Room\nL218: \nL219: The Lord Speaker welcomes the use of the River Room for receptions on behalf of UK-registered charities or cross-party parliamentary events sponsored by members of the Lords\nL220: \nL221:   * 【74†Using the River Room】\nL222: ## Lords enquiry service\nL223: \nL224: Contact 